Rule 1 (input, tensor1, and tensor2 must have identical shapes per dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_3) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∧ shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_3, i)
>>
Rule 2 (out must be a Tensor when provided)
{v_5 : tensor} |= ndim(v_5) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (out tensor must match input tensor in dtype and shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_5 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_5) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_5) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_5, i)
>>
Rule 4 (integer division is disallowed: at least one of tensor1 or tensor2 must be non-integer)
{v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_2) < 1 ∨ dtype_(v_2) > 5) ∨ (dtype_(v_3) < 1 ∨ dtype_(v_3) > 5)
